154	// adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto reads any pending review marker and applies it
155	// to the given session state. Returns (newState, modified, error). If the
156	// state already has Kind set (e.g., a subsequent turn of a review session),
157	// the marker is left in place and modified=false — adoption only happens on
158	// first tag. The marker is cleared on successful first adoption.
159	//
160	// Scoping rules — the marker is left untouched (not cleared) when a scope
161	// mismatch still leaves open the possibility that a future session could
162	// legitimately claim it:
163	//
164	//   - WorktreePath: a Claude session in worktree A must not claim a marker
165	//     meant for a session `entire review` spawned in worktree B. Both
166	//     worktrees share the same .git/entire-sessions/ directory.
167	//   - AgentName: a cursor session must not claim a marker that records a
168	//     claude-code review — the review config and skills are agent-specific,
169	//     and whichever session fires its UserPromptSubmit hook first would
170	//     otherwise silently steal the wrong agent's review metadata.
171	//
172	// StartingSHA is different: once HEAD moves past the marker's commit, no
173	// future session will meaningfully match the original review intent.
174	// A stale marker is cleared rather than left to mis-tag a later unrelated
175	// session.
176	//
177	// Pre-fix markers with empty fields fall back to unscoped adoption for
178	// each missing field (backwards compat).
179	func adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto(ctx context.Context, s session.State, agentName types.AgentName) (session.State, bool, error) {
